[b]Description:[/b]
A script to help people with eric's auction
Please forgive me if I forget to update this thread.

[b]Requirements:[/b]
[list][*]Firefox or Chrome with Tampermonkey (or a compatible userscript manager with userscripts enabled)[/list]

[b]Installation:[/b]
[list=1][*]Make sure Tampermonkey is installed (and enabled / allowed to run userscripts in your browser).
[*]Open the GitHub installation link below.
[*]Confirm installation when prompted.[/list]

[b]Link:[/b] The latest version of eric's Auction Helper is available through GitHub (and auto-updates from the same link).
[url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ericericsw/eric-s-auction-helper/main/auction-helper.user.js]Auction Helper v1.4.1[/url]
[url=https://github.com/ericericsw/eric-s-auction-helper]Repo Link[/url]

[b]Features:[/b]
[list][*]Adds a selection checkbox next to each auction item in eric's Auto Equip Auction threads and highlights selected rows
[*]Displays an inline editable bid badge next to each selected item in the post with real-time two-way sync to the floating panel
[*]Collapsible floating Auction Bid Helper panel with bilingual UI switching (English / 中文)
[*]Parses and validates bid amounts (k / m / b shorthand, whole Credits, and start / cancel / mybid commands) and checks against each item's reserve (start) price
[*]Calculates total Credits across all valid selected items
[*]One-click buttons to copy Recipient (HVEquipAuction), Subject (Auction Bid), and formatted bid lines, plus [b]Select All[/b] / [b]Clear[/b]
[*]One-click [b]Auto fill in MoogleMail[/b] to open HV MoogleMail in a new tab and auto-fill recipient, subject, and bid lines (also compatible with HV Utils' compose UI)
[*]Automatically detects thread phases (Intake, Bidding, Pending, Close) and freezes mail/copy actions outside Bidding to prevent unnecessary MoogleMails while keeping item selection and price calculation active
[*]Compatible with other forum userscripts (such as localization or equipment enhancers) that rewrite post DOM or item names[/list]

[b]Additional information:[/b]
[list][*]The script only activates in verified eric's Auto Equip Auction threads (matching the official thread title format or shop account HVEquipAuction) that contain auction equipment items.
[*]Checking an item's box selects it with "start" (its reserve price) by default and automatically expands the panel if collapsed.
[*]You can edit bid amounts either in the floating panel or directly inside the inline badge next to the item in the post (Enter or Esc finishes inline editing).
[*]In the floating panel, clicking an item's name smoothly scrolls to and flashes that item in the post, while clicking the external link button next to the item ID opens its equipment stats page in a new tab.
[*]Selected items, bid inputs, panel collapsed state, and language preference are saved in browser/userscript storage, so reloading the thread keeps your draft.
[*]Clicking [b]Auto fill in MoogleMail[/b] also copies the bid lines to your clipboard and opens MoogleMail pre-filled—just review the message and click [b]Send[/b] yourself.
[*]Tampermonkey automatically checks the GitHub install link for future updates (or you can trigger [b]Check for userscript updates[/b] in the Tampermonkey menu).[/list]

[b]History:[/b]
[list][*][url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ericericsw/eric-s-auction-helper/v1.4.1/auction-helper.user.js]1.4.1[/url]: Fixed duplicate checkboxes and orphaned inline badges caused by Hentaiverse localization scripts stripping span tags
[*][url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ericericsw/eric-s-auction-helper/v1.4.0/auction-helper.user.js]1.4.0[/url]: Made the inline bid badge next to selected items directly editable with real-time two-way sync to the floating panel
[*][url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ericericsw/eric-s-auction-helper/v1.3.1/auction-helper.user.js]1.3.1[/url]: Prevented equipment selection failure when other scripts rewrite post DOM (added MutationObserver reconciliation, event delegation, and live item name/color syncing)
[*][url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ericericsw/eric-s-auction-helper/v1.3.0/auction-helper.user.js]1.3.0[/url]: Added thread phase detection (Intake / Pending / Close) to freeze mail & copy actions outside Bidding while keeping selection and price calculation active
[*][url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ericericsw/eric-s-auction-helper/v1.2.0/auction-helper.user.js]1.2.0[/url]: Initial GitHub release with item checkboxes, inline bid badges, collapsible EN/中文 floating panel, bid validation, clipboard copy, and MoogleMail auto-fill[/list]
